  { q: "Who can apply for an income certificate in UP?", a: "Any resident of Uttar Pradesh can apply. The application is usually made in the name of the person whose income needs to be certified — for a student's scholarship, parents often apply in their own name because the family's income is what gets assessed. Aadhaar and a mobile number linked to Aadhaar are required for the eSathi account." },
  { q: "How much does an income certificate cost in UP?", a: "Applying yourself on eSathi costs ₹10–15 as the government fee. If you apply through a CSC (Jan Seva Kendra), you pay ₹30 plus a facilitation charge of roughly ₹30–50. No other charge is official — do not pay agents more than this." },
  { q: "How long is a UP income certificate valid?", a: "An income certificate issued in Uttar Pradesh is generally valid for 3 years from the date of issue. Some schemes or institutions ask for a certificate from the current financial year, so check the requirement of the scheme you are applying to before reusing an old certificate." },
  { q: "How many days does it take to get an income certificate?", a: "The normal processing time is 7–15 working days. The Lekhpal's field verification is the slowest stage. During the July–September scholarship season, applications surge and files can take longer, so apply well before any deadline." },
